Use realpath() instead of canonicalize_file_name().

canonicalize_file_name() is a GNU C library extension; realpath() with a
NULL buffer is the POSIX.1-2008 function it is documented to be equivalent
to, and is what C libraries without the extension (LikeOS's) offer.  The
result is still a malloc'd string freed by the caller.

